  "merger_description": "Accenture Venture Holdings, LLC, an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Accenture plc (together with its direct and indirect subsidiaries, **Accenture**) proposes to acquire approximately 80% to 90% of the shares in (and control of) Dragos, Inc. (together with its direct and indirect subsidiaries, including Phosphorus Security LLC (**Phosphorus**), **Dragos**).\n\nAccenture is a global professional services company headquartered in Dublin, Ireland. It provides a broad range of services across strategy, consulting, digital, technology, and operations designed to assist public and private clients.\n\nAccenture provides a range of services in the cybersecurity space from strategic planning through managed security services, operating as both a strategic consultant and systems integrator, working with technology solution partners to offer full-service offerings to customers.\n\nDragos is a global supplier of Operational Technology (**OT**) cybersecurity asset discovery, vulnerability management and threat detection technology, as well as threat intelligence and related services. Its subsidiary, Phosphorus, provides extended Internet of Things (**xIoT**) device discovery, vulnerability identification and remediation technology. Dragos is headquartered in the US.\n\nAccenture has separately notified its proposed acquisition of runZero, Inc (MN-60031), which the ACCC is also assessing.",
